{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-110180","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177217","text":"The first reply that was only its title — 2026-09-18"}]},{"id":"blk-110181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177218","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: the page refuses such a reply and restores the draft, driven on a real screen against a local provider fixture (16 held · 0 failed); and the CAUSE is now reproduced and measured — the model's first structured call can carry only the opening title header. A second defect the stream exposed, a streaming accumulator never reset between tool calls, is fixed here too."},{"id":"spn-177219","text":" Finding 1 of "},{"id":"spn-177220","marks":["code"],"text":"REVIEW_EVIDENCE_RULINGS_2026_09_18.md"},{"id":"spn-177221","text":" "},{"id":"spn-177222","marks":["italic"],"text":"After the install"},{"id":"spn-177223","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-110182","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177224","text":"What was measured"}]},{"id":"blk-110183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177225","text":"Driving the cancelled-fold round ("},{"id":"spn-177226","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs/cancelled-fold/driver-attempt2-title-only.log"},{"id":"spn-177227","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177228","marks":["code"],"text":"attempt2-reply-title-only.png"},{"id":"spn-177229","text":"), opus[1m] at xhigh, a "},{"id":"spn-177230","marks":["bold"],"text":"new"},{"id":"spn-177231","text":" conversation ("},{"id":"spn-177232","marks":["code"],"text":"#bot-new"},{"id":"spn-177233","text":"), the request that later produced the proposal:"}]},{"id":"blk-110184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177234","text":"Thinking · 150 tokens → Preparing reply → Receiving 52 bytes → 78 bytes → Reply received   (25 s)"}]},{"id":"blk-110185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177235","text":"The structured "},{"id":"spn-177236","marks":["code"],"text":"text"},{"id":"spn-177237","text":" was exactly 78 bytes:"}]},{"id":"blk-110186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177238","text":"— the requested header, never closed, no note, no "},{"id":"spn-177239","marks":["code"],"text":"propose_file_edit"},{"id":"spn-177240","text":". The page landed it as a normal reply (\"Reply received.\", the sidebar row "},{"id":"spn-177241","marks":["italic"],"text":"Ready"},{"id":"spn-177242","text":"), so the driver found no card and the round produced nothing. The same request resent in that conversation — now titled by nothing, so "},{"id":"spn-177243","marks":["code"],"text":"titleSource"},{"id":"spn-177244","text":" was "},{"id":"spn-177245","marks":["code"],"text":"fallback"},{"id":"spn-177246","text":" and the title was "},{"id":"spn-177247","marks":["bold"],"text":"asked for again"},{"id":"spn-177248","text":" — answered in 92 s with the proposal. (The title instruction rides in "},{"id":"spn-177249","marks":["code"],"text":"bot_instructions"},{"id":"spn-177250","text":", which "},{"id":"spn-177251","marks":["code"],"text":"bots.rs"},{"id":"spn-177252","text":" folds into the stdin prompt under \"User-configured conversational role\"; the "},{"id":"spn-177253","marks":["code"],"text":"--system-prompt"},{"id":"spn-177254","text":" is fixed. The CLI implements "},{"id":"spn-177255","marks":["code"],"text":"--json-schema"},{"id":"spn-177256","text":" as one "},{"id":"spn-177257","marks":["code"],"text":"StructuredOutput"},{"id":"spn-177258","text":" tool the model must call once at the end of its reply, with a nudge and a retry cap when it does not; "},{"id":"spn-177259","marks":["code"],"text":"decode_reply"},{"id":"spn-177260","text":" keeps only the "},{"id":"spn-177261","marks":["code"],"text":"structured_output"},{"id":"spn-177262","text":" object.)"}]},{"id":"blk-110187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177263","text":"Why the model stopped inside the header is not known. n = 1."}]},{"id":"blk-110188","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177264","text":"What changed (page only)"}]},{"id":"blk-110189","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177265","marks":["code"],"text":"conversation-title.js"},{"id":"spn-177266","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-177267","marks":["code"],"text":"conversationReply"},{"id":"spn-177268","text":" also accepts a header the"}]}],"id":"blk-110190","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177269","text":"model opened and never closed "},{"id":"spn-177270","marks":["bold"],"text":"when nothing follows it"},{"id":"spn-177271","text":", yielding the title and an empty text; a header that prose follows without closing is left alone (that reply has an answer in it). New "},{"id":"spn-177272","marks":["code"],"text":"emptyFirstReply(titled, actions)"},{"id":"spn-177273","text":": no prose after the header and no proposal."}]},{"id":"blk-110193","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177274","marks":["code"],"text":"bots.js"},{"id":"spn-177275","text":" — after decoding, a first reply that is empty by that rule"}]}],"id":"blk-110194","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177276","marks":["bold"],"text":"records the title"},{"id":"spn-177277","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-177278","marks":["code"],"text":"titleSource: ai"},{"id":"spn-177279","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-177280","marks":["code"],"text":"attempted"},{"id":"spn-177281","text":" when there was none to keep — either way the resend does not ask again) and then "},{"id":"spn-177282","marks":["bold"],"text":"fails the turn like any other failed reply"},{"id":"spn-177283","text":": the draft and attachments are restored, the transcript says "},{"id":"spn-177284","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"The reply stopped at its title header and carried no answer and no proposal. Your message is restored — send it again in this conversation.\""},{"id":"spn-177285","text":", and nothing is landed as an answer. Both landing paths (the conversation on screen, and a reply landing while another is open) go through the same throw."}]},{"id":"blk-110197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177286","text":"This turns a lost round into one resend, which is the workaround the driver found by hand. It does not prevent the model from doing it again."}]},{"id":"blk-110198","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177287","text":"Driven on a real screen — "},{"id":"spn-177288","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/first-reply-title-only-smoke.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-110199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177289","text":"The decode and the guard run on "},{"id":"spn-177290","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-177291","text":" reply, whatever the provider ("},{"id":"spn-177292","marks":["code"],"text":"bots.js"},{"id":"spn-177293","text":" applies them to the result of "},{"id":"spn-177294","marks":["code"],"text":"bot_chat"},{"id":"spn-177295","text":"), so the measured reply shape can be produced by a local HTTP provider fixture and the Claude CLI is not needed to prove what the page does with it. Real cockpit, throwaway world, an "},{"id":"spn-177296","marks":["code"],"text":"ollama"},{"id":"spn-177297","text":" endpoint pointed at a fixture that records what each request asked for: "},{"id":"spn-177298","marks":["bold"],"text":"16 held · 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-177299","text":" (screenshots in "},{"id":"spn-177300","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs/title-only/shots/"},{"id":"spn-177301","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-110200","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177302","text":"The first send "},{"id":"spn-177303","marks":["bold"],"text":"asks"},{"id":"spn-177304","text":" for a title (the instruction reaches the provider"}]}],"id":"blk-110201","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-110203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177305","text":"inside the system message). The fixture answers with the measured shape — "},{"id":"spn-177306","marks":["code"],"text":"<conversation-title>…"},{"id":"spn-177307","text":" unterminated, nothing after it, no tool call."}]},{"id":"blk-110204","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177308","text":"Nothing lands as an assistant reply: the transcript holds the user message"}]}],"id":"blk-110205","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-110207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177309","text":"and an "},{"id":"spn-177310","marks":["italic"],"text":"App result"},{"id":"spn-177311","text":" carrying the refusal, the status line carries the same sentence, "},{"id":"spn-177312","marks":["bold"],"text":"the draft is restored in the composer"},{"id":"spn-177313","text":", and the conversation is titled from the header ("},{"id":"spn-177314","marks":["code"],"text":"01-title-only-refused.png"},{"id":"spn-177315","text":"; the Activity rail reads "},{"id":"spn-177316","marks":["italic"],"text":"Reply stopped · No live assistant text received"},{"id":"spn-177317","text":" and the sidebar row "},{"id":"spn-177318","marks":["italic"],"text":"Needs attention"},{"id":"spn-177319","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-110208","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177320","text":"The resend "},{"id":"spn-177321","marks":["bold"],"text":"does not ask for a title again"},{"id":"spn-177322","text":" — proven from the fixture's"}]}],"id":"blk-110209","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-110211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177323","text":"own record of the second request — lands a normal reply, empties the composer, and leaves the kept title alone ("},{"id":"spn-177324","marks":["code"],"text":"02-resend-landed.png"},{"id":"spn-177325","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-110212","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177326","text":"The same unterminated header "},{"id":"spn-177327","marks":["bold"],"text":"carrying a proposal"},{"id":"spn-177328","text":" is not refused: it"}]}],"id":"blk-110213","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-110215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177329","text":"lands with its proposal card on screen, title taken from the header too ("},{"id":"spn-177330","marks":["code"],"text":"03-header-with-proposal-lands.png"},{"id":"spn-177331","text":"). The guard is about emptiness, not about the header."}]},{"id":"blk-110216","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177332","text":"A properly closed header still yields the title and the prose."}]}],"id":"blk-110217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-110219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177333","text":"One observation, not changed: the status line and the result entry read "},{"id":"spn-177334","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Error: The reply stopped…\""},{"id":"spn-177335","text":". Every in-page refusal in "},{"id":"spn-177336","marks":["code"],"text":"bots.js"},{"id":"spn-177337","text":" renders through "},{"id":"spn-177338","marks":["code"],"text":"String(error)"},{"id":"spn-177339","text":" and so carries that prefix (the attachment limits, the model catalog, the missing API key). Dropping it is a one-line change to how that file renders "},{"id":"spn-177340","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-177341","text":" failure, so it is left for the owner rather than made here for one message."}]},{"id":"blk-110220","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177342","text":"The cause, measured — 2026-09-18 evening, once the sign-in was restored"}]},{"id":"blk-110221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177343","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs/title-only/run.mjs"},{"id":"spn-177344","text":" replays the turn outside the cockpit with the same flags, schema and prompt assembly, against the same request and pre-fix file, with bt_0034's real role and instructions, and keeps the "},{"id":"spn-177345","marks":["bold"],"text":"full stream-json"},{"id":"spn-177346","text":" the cockpit never keeps. Three runs, opus[1m] at xhigh:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-110223","spans":[{"id":"spn-177347","text":"run"}]},{"id":"blk-110224","spans":[{"id":"spn-177348","text":"title asked"}]},{"id":"blk-110225","spans":[{"id":"spn-177349","text":"turns"}]},{"id":"blk-110226","spans":[{"id":"spn-177350","text":"prose block"}]},{"id":"blk-110227","spans":[{"id":"spn-177351","text":"what happened"}]}],"id":"blk-110222","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-110228","spans":[{"id":"spn-177352","text":"T1"}]},{"id":"blk-110229","spans":[{"id":"spn-177353","text":"yes"}]},{"id":"blk-110230","spans":[{"id":"spn-177354","text":"3"}]},{"id":"blk-110231","spans":[{"id":"spn-177355","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-110232","spans":[{"id":"spn-177356","marks":["bold"],"text":"the failure, reproduced on the first try"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110233","spans":[{"id":"spn-177357","text":"T2"}]},{"id":"blk-110234","spans":[{"id":"spn-177358","text":"yes"}]},{"id":"blk-110235","spans":[{"id":"spn-177359","text":"2"}]},{"id":"blk-110236","spans":[{"id":"spn-177360","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-110237","spans":[{"id":"spn-177361","text":"one complete call"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110238","spans":[{"id":"spn-177362","text":"C1"}]},{"id":"blk-110239","spans":[{"id":"spn-177363","text":"no"}]},{"id":"blk-110240","spans":[{"id":"spn-177364","text":"2"}]},{"id":"blk-110241","spans":[{"id":"spn-177365","text":"2 942 bytes"}]},{"id":"blk-110242","spans":[{"id":"spn-177366","text":"one complete call"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-110243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177367","marks":["bold"],"text":"T1 is the cause."},{"id":"spn-177368","text":" The model's FIRST "},{"id":"spn-177369","marks":["code"],"text":"StructuredOutput"},{"id":"spn-177370","text":" call was 92 bytes and carried one key:"}]},{"id":"blk-110244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177371","text":"{\"text\": \"<conversation-title>Persist Cancelled plans fold state on record pages (dt_0069)\"}"}]},{"id":"blk-110245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177372","text":"The title header, unterminated, and nothing else — the exact 79-character shape Super was left with on 2026-09-18. The CLI refused it against the schema, "},{"id":"spn-177373","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Output does not match required schema: root: must have required property `actions`\""},{"id":"spn-177374","text":", fed that back as a tool result, and the model's second call was the complete answer: the closed title, 2 832 bytes of prose, and a "},{"id":"spn-177375","marks":["code"],"text":"propose_file_edit"},{"id":"spn-177376","text":" of 13 693 bytes. 85 seconds, and the person would have got a correct reply."}]},{"id":"blk-110246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177377","text":"So the model does sometimes end a call having written only the opening header. "},{"id":"spn-177378","marks":["bold"],"text":"What decided the 09-18 outcome was `actions`."},{"id":"spn-177379","text":" Super's "},{"id":"spn-177380","marks":["code"],"text":"bots.rs"},{"id":"spn-177381","text":" requires "},{"id":"spn-177382","marks":["code"],"text":"actions"},{"id":"spn-177383","text":" to be an array and refuses the reply outright when it is not, so the call that reached the page must have carried "},{"id":"spn-177384","marks":["code"],"text":"actions: []"},{"id":"spn-177385","text":" — schema-valid, nothing for the CLI to refuse, nothing upstream to retry. The same premature call is caught when it omits "},{"id":"spn-177386","marks":["code"],"text":"actions"},{"id":"spn-177387","text":" and lands as an empty reply when it includes an empty one. "},{"id":"spn-177388","marks":["bold"],"text":"No schema can express \"the text must be more than its own header\", which is why the page-side guard is the fix and not a workaround."}]},{"id":"blk-110247","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177389","text":"Two observations that are "},{"id":"spn-177390","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-177391","text":" established, at n = 2 and n = 1:"}]},{"id":"blk-110248","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177392","text":"One of the two title-requesting runs made the premature call. That is a"}]}],"id":"blk-110249","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177393","text":"reproduction, not a rate."}]},{"id":"blk-110252","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177394","text":"Only the run that was "},{"id":"spn-177395","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-177396","text":" asked for a title wrote a prose block at all"}]}],"id":"blk-110253","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177397","text":"(2 942 bytes) before its tool call; both title-requesting runs emitted no "},{"id":"spn-177398","marks":["code"],"text":"text_delta"},{"id":"spn-177399","text":" and wrote straight into the schema. Suggestive that the instruction changes the shape of the turn; one control is not a finding."}]},{"id":"blk-110256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177400","text":"Summaries and the complete streams are in "},{"id":"spn-177401","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs/title-only/runs/"},{"id":"spn-177402","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-110257","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177403","text":"A second defect the stream exposed, and its fix"}]},{"id":"blk-110258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177404","marks":["code"],"text":"ReplyState.partial"},{"id":"spn-177405","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-177406","marks":["code"],"text":"claude_connection.rs"},{"id":"spn-177407","text":" is one raw-JSON accumulator for the whole turn, and "},{"id":"spn-177408","marks":["bold"],"text":"nothing reset it between tool calls"},{"id":"spn-177409","text":". T1 streamed two "},{"id":"spn-177410","marks":["code"],"text":"StructuredOutput"},{"id":"spn-177411","text":" calls, so the buffer held "},{"id":"spn-177412","marks":["code"],"text":"{…}{…}"},{"id":"spn-177413","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-177414","marks":["code"],"text":"structured_prefix"},{"id":"spn-177415","text":" kept parsing the FIRST object — the abandoned header. Replaying T1's own deltas through the accumulator: what the page would have shown for the whole turn is the 79-character header, while the reply being written was 2 832 bytes plus a 13.7 KB proposal. The person watches "},{"id":"spn-177416","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Receiving Claude reply… 79 bytes\""},{"id":"spn-177417","text":" sit still for about a minute, then the right answer appears at the end."}]},{"id":"blk-110259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177418","text":"Fixed in "},{"id":"spn-177419","marks":["code"],"text":"observe_reply"},{"id":"spn-177420","text":": a "},{"id":"spn-177421","marks":["code"],"text":"content_block_start"},{"id":"spn-177422","text":" whose block is a "},{"id":"spn-177423","marks":["code"],"text":"tool_use"},{"id":"spn-177424","text":" clears the accumulator, because a new tool call is a new structured reply. "},{"id":"spn-177425","marks":["code"],"text":"a_refused_structured_reply_does_not_freeze_the_one_that_replaces_it"},{"id":"spn-177426","text":" pins it (and that the argument side still never crosses); with the clear disabled the test fails with the stale header, which is how it was checked."}]},{"id":"blk-110260","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177427","text":"Not done"}]},{"id":"blk-110261","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177428","text":"**Whether the title should move out of "},{"id":"spn-177429","marks":["code"],"text":"text"},{"id":"spn-177430","text":" into its own optional schema"}]}],"id":"blk-110262","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177431","text":"field.** The measurement sharpens the case rather than settling it: the model writes the header as a "},{"id":"spn-177432","marks":["italic"],"text":"prefix of the prose"},{"id":"spn-177433","text":", so a call that ends early leaves something that reads like a reply. With its own field an early call would leave "},{"id":"spn-177434","marks":["code"],"text":"text: \"\""},{"id":"spn-177435","text":", which is obviously nothing. It does not remove the premature call, only its disguise, and it touches the Rust schema for both local providers. Still the owner's call."}]},{"id":"blk-110265","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177436","text":"A rate for the premature call. Two title-requesting runs, one of them"}]}],"id":"blk-110266","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177437","text":"premature, is not one."}]},{"id":"blk-110269","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177438","text":"The failing shape has not been produced "},{"id":"spn-177439","marks":["bold"],"text":"through Super's own UI"},{"id":"spn-177440","text":" against"}]}],"id":"blk-110270","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177441","text":"the real provider — only outside it. The page-side guard is covered by "},{"id":"spn-177442","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/first-reply-title-only-smoke.mjs"},{"id":"spn-177443","text":" instead, which drives the identical reply shape through a fixture provider."}]},{"id":"blk-110273","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177444","text":"After the install — 2026-09-19 01:05Z"}]},{"id":"blk-110274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177445","text":"The streaming fix is installed: "},{"id":"spn-177446","marks":["code"],"text":"2db9d36"},{"id":"spn-177447","text":" built in "},{"id":"spn-177448","marks":["code"],"text":"~/build